1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,500
AI systems trained on synthetic data
lose their grounding in human experience.

2
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,500
The current alignment landscape
treats this as something to promise.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,000
We treat it as something to prove.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:21,500
The HumanAI Convention is a governance
layer for AI decisions.

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Gemma 4 receives a scenario and calls
five governance tools —

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
wellbeing, consent, PRISM, NLA,
and a Merkle receipt.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,500
It produces a cryptographically
anchored audit trail.

8
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,000
We demonstrate it on three real cases.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
A rural clinic. A classroom.
A deforestation enforcement system.

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,500
Our framework promoted a 200-line
deterministic guard in front of Gemma 4.

11
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:01,000
Thirteen predeclared, non-compensatory gates.
All passed. Anchored.

12
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:08,000
Ten consecutive fine-tuning candidates
failed those same gates.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
We did not relax the gates.
We published the negative verdicts.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The framework correctly rejected
its own model.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,500
Discipline that holds under its own pressure.

16
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:31,000
You can verify all of this in under a minute.

17
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Fork this public Kaggle kernel and run it.

18
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:44,000
It replays the guard against the canonical
attack set and emits a SHA3 receipt.

19
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,500
We do not ask you to trust us.

20
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:56,000
What we have shipped is the runtime layer.

21
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The grounding interviewer is designed to be
invoked as a function-calling tool

22
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,000
from inside any frontier chat —
Claude, Gemini, or GPT.

23
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Three modes. On user request.
On automatic high-stakes trigger.

24
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Or on opt-in random sampling.

25
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Every invocation produces a verifiable receipt.

26
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,500
The integration spec is public. We are
looking for the first deployment partner.

27
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:30,000
humanaiconvention.com.
The Convention is open.
